{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\comp\\084.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "awaz e ingilab.com", "conf": 0.862, "box": [[302, 10], [620, 8], [620, 41], [302, 44]]}, {"text": "4.4ScratchCodeBlocks", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[316, 87], [656, 89], [656, 119], [316, 117]]}, {"text": "4.4.1Workingwith Scratch CodeBlocks", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[77, 131], [537, 130], [537, 157], [77, 158]]}, {"text": "Blocks are the commands that are used to create programmes in scratch, these are'Drag", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[75, 169], [877, 178], [877, 208], [75, 199]]}, {"text": "n Drop' blocks which allow the user to write programmes without typing commands.", "conf": 0.948, "box": [[75, 207], [876, 213], [876, 243], [75, 237]]}, {"text": "There are a number of block types like motion, looks, sounds, etc. These blocks can be", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[77, 244], [875, 249], [875, 276], [77, 271]]}, {"text": "found on the left most of the screen in Blocks Palette. Clicking on each block category", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[76, 276], [874, 285], [874, 316], [76, 306]]}, {"text": "reveals the command blocks related to that block. A user can drag and drop blocks in the", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[77, 315], [874, 321], [874, 347], [77, 342]]}, {"text": "middle to make a programme. These blocks can be joined over or under other blocks to", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[77, 352], [874, 356], [874, 382], [77, 378]]}, {"text": "make a group; grouped blocks can be moved together by dragging.", "conf": 0.94, "box": [[77, 385], [677, 389], [677, 420], [77, 416]]}, {"text": "Try to drag'point towards'block in the middle,and then click it. Notice the sprite turns", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[81, 434], [872, 436], [872, 463], [81, 461]]}, {"text": "towards the mouse pointer regardless of its position. However, if you use 'glide' block", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[79, 468], [871, 469], [871, 496], [79, 494]]}, {"text": "instead, the sprite moves towards the mouse pointer or towards a random position; in", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[79, 503], [869, 504], [869, 530], [79, 529]]}, {"text": "thenumberofsecondsmentioned.", "conf": 0.957, "box": [[81, 539], [395, 539], [395, 562], [81, 562]]}, {"text": "The block'change y by' and 'change x by' move the sprite in terms of the mentioned", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[77, 579], [870, 577], [870, 607], [77, 609]]}, {"text": "stepsinyandxaxis,respectively.", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[79, 616], [378, 616], [378, 642], [79, 642]]}, {"text": "aecenpceition", "conf": 0.681, "box": [[520, 673], [611, 670], [611, 688], [521, 690]]}, {"text": "changeyby", "conf": 0.821, "box": [[703, 673], [787, 673], [787, 694], [703, 694]]}, {"text": "m.tbwards", "conf": 0.626, "box": [[104, 677], [175, 677], [175, 691], [104, 691]]}, {"text": "20", "conf": 0.644, "box": [[806, 675], [824, 675], [824, 688], [806, 688]]}, {"text": "4.4.2Changingpositionof Spritesviacode", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[79, 741], [562, 739], [562, 766], [79, 769]]}, {"text": "A user can change the position of the sprite by using'go to'command.There are two", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[78, 782], [868, 782], [868, 808], [78, 808]]}, {"text": "variants of'go to':", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[79, 815], [246, 815], [246, 841], [79, 841]]}, {"text": "'go to random position' which takes the sprite to a random position on screen;", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[102, 858], [869, 862], [869, 891], [102, 888]]}, {"text": "when clicked ittakes thespritetoarandompositionon theoutputarea.", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[105, 895], [750, 899], [749, 922], [105, 918]]}, {"text": "takes the sprite to a fixed location as provided in the code block. A user can change", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[101, 972], [865, 974], [865, 1000], [101, 998]]}, {"text": "coordinatestoseetheeffect.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[103, 1007], [363, 1007], [363, 1030], [103, 1030]]}, {"text": "-36", "conf": 0.748, "box": [[377, 1071], [410, 1071], [410, 1095], [377, 1095]]}, {"text": "-73", "conf": 0.747, "box": [[300, 1074], [330, 1074], [330, 1094], [300, 1094]]}, {"text": "go to ~ random position", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[527, 1070], [713, 1062], [714, 1090], [528, 1098]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.843, "box": [[90, 1153], [185, 1153], [185, 1170], [90, 1170]]}, {"text": "79", "conf": 0.512, "box": [[455, 1163], [483, 1163], [483, 1183], [455, 1183]]}, {"text": "ComputerScience Grade-7", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[222, 1164], [391, 1162], [391, 1182], [222, 1184]]}, {"text": "Unit4:Programming", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[585, 1163], [709, 1163], [709, 1180], [585, 1180]]}]}